nsecutive reviews proved that identity was attesting structurally invalid objects, and a fuzz task cannot honestly pass while the gate it fuzzes admits what the contract rejects. The scope field is updated to say so rather than leaving the task pretending to be narrower than it is. Splitting the work into a new task was considered and rejected because the validator is already in flight in this candidate. Method requirement for this rework: the previous two rounds each fixed exactly the fields the reviewer named and were then defeated by the next unenumerated field. Do not repeat that. Enumerate every declared constraint in the pinned Sections 10.1-10.4 systematically from SPEC.md, record the enumeration as evidence, and implement against that list. Reviewer finding F2 also stands: README claimed a completed audit that had not happened, so claims must be reproducible through both public entries or removed."}}]},{"version":"activity-event.v1","id":"AEV-260831-4e1dd905b5f5760b22bca398","sequence":79,"timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:35:39.18601Z","actor":{"principal":{"availability":"unknown"},"agent":{"availability":"known","value":"claude"},"run":{"availability":"unknown"},"session":{"availability":"known","value":"6d2e8b01-2cc4-4e49-994a-05938b6ce680"},"operator":{"availability":"unknown"}},"subject":{"element_id":"TASK-260830-8x76g1","element_type":"task"},"source":{"kind":"local_cli","entrypoint":"cmd.runMutate","request":{"availability":"unknown"}},"correlation_id":"COR-260831-2aecee5aff113546e06b6e17","causal_order":1,"operation":"content","changes":[{"field":"scope","before":{"kind":"text","text":"relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.5.0 (commit 28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c); §1.6, §10.1-10.4, §17.3. Work only inside the common-types-and-canonical-identities story boundary."},"after":{"kind":"text","text":"relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.5.0 (commit 28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c); Sections 1.6, 10.1-10.4, 17.3. This task grew beyo