58:{"timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:36:32.891Z","ordinal":57,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0591b-1f95-7943-a69e-e6707d41e923","turn_id":"01a0591b-218e-7791-8c1d-c09fdfe98b6c","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-a5bba049-883e-426e-a7af-ebf80e9db7ae","process_id":"80279","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","task-board q --format compact 'get(TASK-260830-8x76g1) { overview checklist notes preconditionResources outcomeResources review }'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-2wdm5e/worktree","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"task-board q --format compact 'get(TASK-260830-8x76g1) { overview checklist notes preconditionResources outcomeResources review }'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"id:TASK-260830-8x76g1\nname:fuzz-common-types-and-canonicalization\nstatus:development\nassignee:[implementer] developer (codex)\nparent:STORY-260830-2wdm5e\nchecklist:[{\"text\":\"Production entry points implement the scoped deliverable: Prove recursive closed shapes, Unicode ordering, invalid dates, malformed identifiers, and cross-platform golden identities\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Relevant positive, negative, compatibility, and recovery tests pass with logs attached\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"README/doctor/capability evidence and specification traceability are updated without unsupported claims\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Go native fuzz targets cover scalar parsing and JCS canonicalization at production entry points, with a committed seed corpus derived from the shapes prior reviews found: leap seconds, lowercase RFC3339, Windows reserved device names and wildcards, unpaired surrogates, and duplicate or non-string map keys\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Canonicalization is proven round-trip stable and order-independent under fuzz: the identity digest of an object is invariant under key reordering and insignificant whitespace, and no input causes a panic or an accepted value that later refuses\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Fuzz runs are bounded and deterministic in the validation suite: a fixed -fuzztime with a seed corpus, so the configured gate stays reproducible rather than time-dependent\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Code written per task description and AC\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Lint clean\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Implementation matches AC\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Solution fits project architecture\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Tests green\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Gate, refusal, validation, authorization, and attestation behavior attacked, not read — positive-path-only evidence is not accepted\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"If review does not accept the work — verdict evidence added and status routed by the explicit verdict branches\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Scoped closed-shape validation exists for Sections 10.1-10.4 and is invoked on the composed production path before identity is calculated or verified: exact top-level and nested member sets, and BlobChunk index/offset/size order, bounds and coverage invariants, with the composed call site named in evidence\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Negative tests and fuzz corpus cover an unknown top-level member, an unknown nested member, invalid chunk bounds/order/coverage, and closed Transfer Manifest nested shapes; each must make identity calculation and verification refuse rather than attest\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"tracecheck -section 17.3 passes for the implemented identity contribution without claiming migration publication or atomic-reference behavior that README correctly reports unavailable\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"AUDIT, not spot-fix: every open or extension point in closed_shapes.go validates its full key grammar per Section 1.6, and every string[n..m] bound counts Unicode characters rather than UTF-8 bytes; both directions are proven, an invalid key of any namespace is refused and a valid multibyte value at the character bound is accepted\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Every fuzz target the candidate defines is invoked by the configured validation suite with a fixed -fuzztime, including the closed-shape target; a newly added target that is not wired into the suite is a gate gap\",\"done\":true},{\"text\":\"Constraints are DERIVED from the pinned SPEC.md Sections 10.1-10.4 by systematic enumeration of every declared member type, character bound, nullability, tagged-union, ordering, uniqueness and cross-field rule reachable at this gate, and the enumeration itself is recorded as evidence; a hand-picked subset is not acceptable\",\"done\":false},{\"text\":\"Nested value rules reuse the production scalar validators rather than looser local grammars, and the normative TM-GIT-N2 stage-4 refusal plus valid multibyte values at each character limit are proven through both CalculateObjectIdentity and VerifyObjectIdentity\",\"done\":false},{\"text\":\"README states only what reproduces through both public identity entries; no completed-audit or coverage claim is made that a reader cannot reproduce\",\"done\":false}]\nnotes:STORY-260830-2wdm5e base refresh SKIPPED: the managed workspace holds uncommitted work, so there was no clean checkpoint branch to replay onto trunk e8f8e2febfbc; the branch is unchanged at fork point c9e5290b1506\\nspawn workload selection: class=implementation source=derived policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=codex/gpt-5.6-sol/high pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:f7130ab6b2ae6c4bf7bde632137d1eb646cbd3be7f4039acc56d0cf5f965b005 rationale=\"Following rank-1 recommendation: fuzzing the scalar and canonicalization boundary is the last leaf of this Story and must find the shapes that targeted review already proved are easy to get wrong.\"\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: exclusive[codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\\nspawn launch composition: empty; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; producer=v1.6.1; diagnostic=launch_composition_empty; no project MCP servers enabled\\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-632326, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-632326)\\nImplemented native scalar/JCS/identity fuzz targets with committed review-derived corpus, recursive malformed-shape refusals, cross-platform identity golden, fixed 100x validation gates, and Test/Fuzz traceability ownership. Full/race/coverage/fuzz/trace/build/vet/cross-build/diff gates exited 0. Coverage: scalar 90.5%, canonicaljson 84.0%, traceability 85.0%. task-board validate exited 0 with 262 inherited MISSING_ACTIVITY diagnostics; current task was not listed. Evidence: TASK-260830-8x76g1_results.md, TASK-260830-8x76g1_validation-logs.tar.gz, TASK-260830-8x76g1_logbook.md. Read-only scope; durable crash recovery is not applicable and no runtime capability is claimed.\\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (codex) (exit=0)\\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-632326, pid=30840, exit=0)\\nspawn workload selection: class=review source=derived policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=codex/gpt-5.6-sol/high pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:d826fb4554b9825b9cea38eb387c522977ecf69d6e6e80c0a3c63c4696a71d0b rationale=\"Following rank-1 recommendation: this is the Story-final candidate, so review must confirm the fuzz targets genuinely exercise production entries, the corpus covers the shapes prior reviews found, and the gate stays deterministic.\"\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: exclusive[codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\\nspawn launch composition: empty; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; producer=v1.6.1; diagnostic=launch_composition_empty; no project MCP servers enabled\\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-c34bb4, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-c34bb4)\\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-c34bb4, pid=4457, exit=0)\\nCR revision 1 blocking finding accepted and it is the most serious defect found in this Story. CalculateObjectIdentity and VerifyObjectIdentity validate generic JSON, common-model numbers, the schema lookup and the self-field digest, but never the selected schemas closed member set or nested contract invariants. The reviewer drove both production entries with three invalid Blob Descriptors: an unknown top-level member, an unknown member inside a nested BlobChunk, and a chunk with index=9 offset=99 size=0 for a one-byte blob. All three received a digest and all three verified. For a content-addressed identity that is a bypass around the check: the system attests an object the closed contract requires the receiver to reject. Rework must add a scoped closed-shape validator for Sections 10.1-10.4 covering exact top-level and nested member sets plus chunk order, bounds and coverage, and it must be invoked on the composed production path rather than tested as an isolated helper. Separately the assigned Section 17.3 still has no scoped implementation owner and must be made traceable without claiming migration publication or atomic-reference behavior that README correctly reports unavailable.\\nSTORY-260830-2wdm5e base refresh SKIPPED: the managed workspace holds uncommitted work, so there was no clean checkpoint branch to replay onto trunk e8f8e2febfbc; the branch is unchanged at fork point c9e5290b1506\\nspawn workload selection: class=implementation source=derived policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=codex/gpt-5.6-sol/high pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:f7130ab6b2ae6c4bf7bde632137d1eb646cbd3be7f4039acc56d0cf5f965b005 rationale=\"Following rank-1 recommendation: identity currently attests objects that violate the pinned closed contract, which is an attestation-integrity defect rather than a missing test.\"\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: exclusive[codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\\nspawn launch composition: empty; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; producer=v1.6.1; diagnostic=launch_composition_empty; no project MCP servers enabled\\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-186ca8, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-186ca8)\\nRework closes CR revision 1 attestation bypass. Production call site prepareObjectIdentity now invokes validateImmutableObjectShape before CalculateObjectIdentity or VerifyObjectIdentity can attest. Exact Blob Descriptor/BlobChunk and recursive Transfer Manifest closed shapes refuse unknown top/nested members and chunk order/bounds/coverage violations; Section 17.3 migrated-from identity contribution is traceable without migration publication or atomic-reference claims. Final standalone gates all exited 0: focused/race/80.7% coverage, three canonical fuzz targets plus scalar fuzz at fixed 100x, scoped tracecheck for 1.6/10.1-10.4/17.3, trace tests, catalog check, full tests/coverage, vet, build, Linux/Windows cross-test builds, diff check, and board validate. Board validate retains 262 inherited MISSING_ACTIVITY diagnostics and does not list this task. Evidence: TASK-260830-8x76g1_rework-results.md, TASK-260830-8x76g1_rework-logbook.md, TASK-260830-8x76g1_rework-validation-logs.tar.gz.\\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (codex) (exit=0)\\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-186ca8, pid=53577, exit=0)\\nspawn workload selection: class=review source=derived policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=codex/gpt-5.6-sol/high pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:d826fb4554b9825b9cea38eb387c522977ecf69d6e6e80c0a3c63c4696a71d0b rationale=\"Following rank-1 recommendation: Story-final candidate, so review must confirm the closed-shape validator is on the composed production path for every scoped schema, refuses without over-refusing valid objects, and that section 17.3 traceability is honest.\"\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: exclusive[codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\\nspawn launch composition: empty; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; producer=v1.6.1; diagnostic=launch_composition_empty; no project MCP servers enabled\\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-5a91c9, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-5a91c9)\\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-5a91c9, pid=14322, exit=0)\\nCR revision 2 review returned three blocking findings and they fall into two mirror classes, so the rework must be an AUDIT rather than three spot fixes. F1 under-validates: validateMigrationExtensionObject inspects only works.relux.ax.migrated-from, so a Transfer Manifest carrying extensions with the key not_namespaced is attested by both CalculateObjectIdentity and VerifyObjectIdentity. F2 over-validates in the opposite direction: Section 1.6 bounds string[n..m] in UTF-8 CHARACTERS and ManifestEntry.target is string[1..4096], but the validator compares len(target) in bytes, so a valid 3999-character 5999-byte target is refused. Do not fix only the two fields the reviewer named. Sweep closed_shapes.go for every open or extension point and validate its full key grammar, and for every string bound switch to character counting consistent with the common scalar contract. Prove both directions at the production entries. F3 is a gate gap in the suite this candidate itself extended: the closed-shape fuzz target is defined but never invoked, so wire every defined target into the configured suite with a fixed -fuzztime.\\nSTORY-260830-2wdm5e base refresh SKIPPED: the managed workspace holds uncommitted work, so there was no clean checkpoint branch to replay onto trunk e8f8e2febfbc; the branch is unchanged at fork point c9e5290b1506\\nspawn workload selection: class=implementation source=derived policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=codex/gpt-5.6-sol/high pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:f7130ab6b2ae6c4bf7bde632137d1eb646cbd3be7f4039acc56d0cf5f965b005 rationale=\"Following rank-1 recommendation: the two findings are mirror classes across the whole validator, so this needs a systematic audit of over- and under-validation rather than two point fixes.\"\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: exclusive[codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\\nspawn launch composition: empty; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; producer=v1.6.1; diagnostic=launch_composition_empty; no project MCP servers enabled\\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-9484d4, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-9484d4)\\nRework revision 3 closes CR rev2 F1-F3 with a shared Section 1.6 extensions validator (full reverse-DNS grammar, 64 members, depth 4, 65536 canonical bytes), Unicode-character string bounds, and a dynamic configured-suite test requiring every repo fuzz target exactly once at fixed 100x/parallel=1. Expected-red focused tests exited 1 before the fix; all post-fix focused/full/race/coverage/four-fuzz/trace/catalog/build/vet/cross-build/JSON/diff/board gates exited 0. Coverage canonicaljson 81.2%, scalar 90.5%. task-board validate retains 262 inherited MISSING_ACTIVITY diagnostics and does not list this task. Evidence: TASK-260830-8x76g1_rework-rev3-results.md, TASK-260830-8x76g1_rework-rev3-logbook.md, TASK-260830-8x76g1_rework-rev3-validation-logs.tar.gz.\\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (codex) (exit=0)\\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-9484d4, pid=22190, exit=0)\\nspawn workload selection: class=review source=derived policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=codex/gpt-5.6-sol/high pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:d826fb4554b9825b9cea38eb387c522977ecf69d6e6e80c0a3c63c4696a71d0b rationale=\"Following rank-1 recommendation: Story-final candidate after a two-directional validator audit; review must attack both over-refusal and under-refusal across every closed shape, not only the three previously named fields.\"\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: exclusive[codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\\nspawn launch composition: empty; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; producer=v1.6.1; diagnostic=launch_composition_empty; no project MCP servers enabled\\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-1ce05f, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-1ce05f)\\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=1)\\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-1ce05f, pid=41711, exit=1)\\nspawn autonomous recovery: run RUN-260831-1ce05f queued successor RUN-260831-0a4533 (attempt 1/3, model=gpt-5.6-sol): spawned agent exited with code 1\\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260831-0a4533)\\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260831-0a4533, pid=61816, exit=0)\\nOrchestrator re-scope after CR revision 3 review. This task began as fuzz coverage and has grown, by successive review findings, into the owner of the scoped Section 10.1-10.4 closed-shape conformance gate. That growth is legitimate: three consecutive reviews proved that identity was attesting structurally invalid objects, and a fuzz task cannot honestly pass while the gate it fuzzes admits what the contract rejects. The scope field is updated to say so rather than leaving the task pretending to be narrower than it is. Splitting the work into a new task was considered and rejected because the validator is already in flight in this candidate. Method requirement for this rework: the previous two rounds each fixed exactly the fields the reviewer named and were then defeated by the next unenumerated field. Do not repeat that. Enumerate every declared constraint in the pinned Sections 10.1-10.4 systematically from SPEC.md, record the enumeration as evidence, and implement against that list. Reviewer finding F2 also stands: README claimed a completed audit that had not happened, so claims must be reproducible through both public entries or removed.\\nSTORY-260830-2wdm5e base refresh SKIPPED: the managed workspace holds uncommitted work, so there was no clean checkpoint branch to replay onto trunk e8f8e2febfbc; the branch is unchanged at fork point c9e5290b1506\\nspawn workload selection: class=implementation source=derived policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=codex/gpt-5.6-sol/high pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:f7130ab6b2ae6c4bf7bde632137d1eb646cbd3be7f4039acc56d0cf5f965b005 rationale=\"Following rank-1 recommendation: two prior rounds were defeated by fixing only the named fields, so this mu