544:{"timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:55:30.588Z","ordinal":543,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0f2b6256657c4564016a95ce00e9a887d2ac488f548b09b434","status":"completed","call_id":"call_MRCt2BlNSRk64L26gpzWGAkr","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-2wdm5e/worktree/.temp/TASK-260830-8x76g1/TASK-260830-8x76g1_rework-rev4-results.md\\n+# TASK-260830-8x76g1 — developer rework revision 4\\n+\\n+## Outcome\\n+\\n+CR revision 3's narrowed recursive Transfer Manifest gate is repaired by a\\n+systematic derivation from pinned SPEC.md Sections 1.6 and 10.1–10.4, rather\\n+than by patching only the seven reviewer examples. The full derivation and the\\n+boundary between candidate-local and referenced-data constraints is recorded\\n+in `TASK-260830-8x76g1_constraint-enumeration.md`.\\n+\\n+Both public entries use the same production call site before calculation or\\n+attestation:\\n+\\n+`CalculateObjectIdentity|VerifyObjectIdentity -> prepareObjectIdentity -> validateImmutableObjectShape`\\n+\\n+## Implemented scope\\n+\\n+- Added production scalar validators for `git-oid`, object-format-bound Git\\n+  OIDs, fully qualified `git-ref`, and sanitized Git URLs; their constructors\\n+  and JSON read/write paths are covered by unit tests and the existing native\\n+  scalar fuzz target.\\n+- Completed candidate-local Transfer Manifest value validation: workspace\\n+  member paths/identities/policies, remote bounds/order/URLs, GitHead union,\\n+  GitObjectPack types, GitIndex version/count/path-stage order/TM-GIT-N2,\\n+  GitIndexEntry scalar/boolean rules, GitFeatures sparse-pair state, Git object\\n+  format consistency, and recursive GitSubmodule nullability, parent gitlink,\\n+  depth 16, total 256, cycle and sibling-path rules.\\n+- Completed reachable ManifestEntry cross-field checks: destination case\\n+  collision, lexical symlink containment, and earlier-file/same-mode hardlink\\n+  targets.\\n+- Enforced the 5,242,880-byte encoded immutable-object maximum before decode.\\n+- Extended deterministic closed-shape fuzz mutations with nested bounds,\\n+  malformed digest/ref/URL, stage 4, impossible submodule state, sparse-pair,\\n+  symlink/hardlink and index-count attacks. The configured suite still invokes\\n+  every repository fuzz target exactly once at fixed `100x`, `parallel=1`.\\n+- Narrowed README claims to self-contained rules reproducible through both\\n+  public entries. Referenced Blob Descriptor/child-manifest/Git pack/index and\\n+  filesystem checks are explicitly not claimed by this package.\\n+\\n+## Negative and boundary evidence\\n+\\n+Before implementation, the focused production-entry regression command exited\\n+`1`: all 21 initial malformed nested values received an identity. The saved\\n+`expected-red-nested-values.log` records that failure.\\n+\\n+After implementation, the focused entry test exits `0` and covers the reviewer\\n+examples plus derived ordering/cross-field rules, exact valid multibyte limits,\\n+recursive depth/count/state, and encoded-size refusal. Exact 256-character\\n+repository/tree/submodule identities, 128-character remote names, 4096-character\\n+symlink targets, and 255-character media types are accepted by both entries;\\n+their over-bound forms refuse. Invalid calendar dates and malformed UUID/digest,\\n+Git OID/ref/URL values refuse before identity calculation and verification.\\n+\\n+## Validation\\n+\\n+Every command below ran as a standalone foreground process. Exit codes are the\\n+actual process results.\\n+\\n+| Gate | Exit | Result |\\n+| --- | ---: | --- |\\n+| Expected-red focused production-entry regression before fix | 1 | Expected failure: 21 nested invalid shapes were attested. |\\n+| Focused production-entry regression after fix | 0 | Pass |\\n+| Cross-platform golden identity + RFC 8785 UTF-16 order | 0 | Pass |\\n+| `go test ./... -count=1` | 0 | Pass |\\n+| `go test ./... -v -count=1` | 0 | Pass |\\n+| `go test ./... -cover -count=1` | 0 | Pass |\\n+| Focused `-race` scalar/canonical tests | 0 | Pass |\\n+| Focused package coverage | 0 | scalar 90.1%; canonicaljson 81.5% |\\n+| `FuzzScalarProductionEntries`, fixed `100x`, `parallel=1` | 0 | Pass |\\n+| `FuzzCanonicalizeRoundTrip`, fixed `100x`, `parallel=1` | 0 | Pass |\\n+| `FuzzObjectIdentityRepresentationInvariant`, fixed `100x`, `parallel=1` | 0 | Pass |\\n+| `FuzzClosedIdentityShapeRefusal`, fixed `100x`, `parallel=1` | 0 | Pass; 48 seed corpus entries loaded |\\n+| Scoped tracecheck 1.6, 10.1–10.4, 17.3 | 0 | `assigned_scopes=6` |\\n+| Catalog generated-output check | 0 | Pass |\\n+| `go build ./...` | 0 | Pass |\\n+| `go vet ./...` | 0 | Pass |\\n+| Linux amd64 canonicaljson test cross-compile | 0 | Pass |\\n+| Windows amd64 canonicaljson test cross-compile | 0 | Pass |\\n+| `gofmt -l internal` | 0 | Empty output |\\n+| `git diff --check` | 0 | Pass |\\n+| `task-board validate` | 0 | 262 inherited `MISSING_ACTIVITY` diagnostics; current task absent |\\n+\\n+## Scope boundary\\n+\\n+This package is read-only and deterministic, so crash/idempotency evidence for\\n+durable mutation is not applicable. Section 17.3 evidence covers only the\\n+immutable migrated-from identity contribution. It does not claim migration\\n+publication, atomic reference advancement, rollback retention, `ax migrate`,\\n+`ax doctor`, or a runtime capability.\\n+\\n*** Add File: /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-2wdm5e/worktree/.temp/TASK-260830-8x76g1/TASK-260830-8x76g1_rework-rev4-logbook.md\\n+# TASK-260830-8x76g1 — rework revision 4 logbook\\n+\\n+- Pinned source read locally from spec commit\\n+  `28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c`; no unpinned specification text\\n+  was used.\\n+- CR revision 3's failure class was broader than its seven examples: member\\n+  names were closed, but most nested values, unions, ordering and cross-field\\n+  rules were not validated.\\n+- Expected-red evidence was captured before implementation. The production\\n+  entry test exited 1 because 21/21 malformed nested candidates were attested.\\n+- Reused `internal/scalar` for path, UUID, timestamp and digest rules; added\\n+  production scalar types for Git OIDs, refs and sanitized URLs rather than\\n+  embedding looser regular expressions in `closed_shapes.go`.\\n+- Kept candidate-local validation separate from facts that require referenced\\n+  bytes: Blob Descriptor equality, child-manifest closure, raw Git pack/index\\n+  agreement, isolated object-database resolution, and filesystem resolution.\\n+  README now states that boundary explicitly.\\n+- The recursive submodule validator now checks initialized/uninitialized state,\\n+  TM-GIT parent index linkage, object formats, depth 16, total 256, ancestor\\n+  cycles and sibling path collisions. Exact depth/count positives and narrowed\\n+  negatives drive both identity entries.\\n+- Every post-fix test/fuzz/trace/build/vet/cross-compile gate exited 0. Package\\n+  coverage is 90.1% scalar and 81.5% canonicaljson.\\n+- `task-board validate` exited 0 while printing 262 inherited\\n+  `MISSING_ACTIVITY` diagnostics. `TASK-260830-8x76g1` is not among them.\\n+- No external blocker, product decision, durable mutation, doctor output, or\\n+  capability advertisement was introduced.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0591b-218e-7791-8c1d-c09fdfe98b6c","create_time":1788202493.775923}}}
545:{"timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:55:30.602Z","ordinal":544,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0591b-1f95-7943-a69e-e6707d41e923","turn_id":"01a0591b-218e-7791-8c1d-c09fdfe98b6c","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-a6d3bb0d-cd58-4b29-93a2-0ed503eb3e05","changes":{"/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-2wdm5e/worktree/.temp/TASK-260830-8x76g1/TASK-260830-8x76g1_rework-rev4-results.md":{"type":"add","content":"# TASK-260830-8x76g1 — developer rework revision 4\n\n## Outcome\n\nCR revision 3's narrowed recursive Transfer Manifest gate is repaired by a\nsystematic derivation from pinned SPEC.md Sections 1.6 and 10.1–10.4, rather\nthan by patching only the seven reviewer examples. The full derivation and the\nboundary between candidate-local and referenced-data constraints is recorded\nin `TASK-260830-8x76g1_constraint-enumeration.md`.\n\nBoth public entries use the same production call site before calculation or\nattestation:\n\n`CalculateObjectIdentity|VerifyObjectIdentity -> prepareObjectIdentity -> validateImmutableObjectShape`\n\n## Implemented scope\n\n- Added production scalar validators for `git-oid`, object-format-bound Git\n  OIDs, fully qualified `git-ref`, and sanitized Git URLs; their constructors\n  and JSON read/write paths are covered by unit tests and the existing native\n  scalar fuzz target.\n- Completed candidate-local Transfer Manifest value validation: workspace\n  member paths/identities/policies, remote bounds/order/URLs, GitHead union,\n  GitObjectPack types, GitIndex version/count/path-stage order/TM-GIT-N2,\n  GitIndexEntry scalar/boolean rules, GitFeatures sparse-pair state, Git object\n  format consistency, and recursive GitSubmodule nullability, parent gitlink,\n  depth 16, total 256, cycle and sibling-path rules.\n- Completed reachable ManifestEntry cross-field checks: destination case\n  collision, lexical symlink containment, and earlier-file/same-mode hardlink\n  targets.\n- Enforced the 5,242,880-byte encoded immutable-object maximum before decode.\n- Extended deterministic closed-shape fuzz mutations with nested bounds,\n  malformed digest/ref/URL, stage 4, impossible submodule state, sparse-pair,\n  symlink/hardlink and index-count attacks. The configured suite still invokes\n  every repository fuzz target exactly once at fixed `100x`, `parallel=1`.\n- Narrowed README claims to self-contained rules reproducible through both\n  public entries. Referenced Blob Descriptor/child-manifest/Git pack/index and\n  filesystem checks are explicitly not claimed by this package.\n\n## Negative and boundary evidence\n\nBefore implementation, the focused production-entry regression command exited\n`1`: all 21 initial malformed nested values received an identity. The saved\n`expected-red-nested-values.log` records that failure.\n\nAfter implementation, the focused entry test exits `0` and covers the reviewer\nexamples plus derived ordering/cross-field rules, exact valid multibyte limits,\nrecursive depth/count/state, and encoded-size refusal. Exact 256-character\nrepository/tree/submodule identities, 128-character remote names, 4096-character\nsymlink targets, and 255-character media types are accepted by both entries;\ntheir over-bound forms refuse. Invalid calendar dates and malformed UUID/digest,\nGit OID/ref/URL values refuse before identity calculation and verification.\n\n## Validation\n\nEvery command below ran as a standalone foreground process. Exit codes are the\nactual process results.\n\n| Gate | Exit | Result |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| Expected-red focused production-entry regression before fix | 1 | Expected failure: 21 nested invalid shapes were attested. |\n| Focused production-entry regression after fix | 0 | Pass |\n| Cross-platform golden identity + RFC 8785 UTF-16 order | 0 | Pass |\n| `go test ./... -count=1` | 0 | Pass |\n| `go test ./... -v -count=1` | 0 | Pass |\n| `go test ./... -cover -count=1` | 0 | Pass |\n| Focused `-race` scalar/canonical tests | 0 | Pass |\n| Focused package coverage | 0 | scalar 90.1%; canonicaljson 81.5% |\n| `FuzzScalarProductionEntries`, fixed `100x`, `parallel=1` | 0 | Pass |\n| `FuzzCanonicalizeRoundTrip`, fixed `100x`, `parallel=1` | 0 | Pass |\n| `FuzzObjectIdentityRepresentationInvariant`, fixed `100x`, `parallel=1` | 0 | Pass |\n| `FuzzClosedIdentityShapeRefusal`, fixed `100x`, `parallel=1` | 0 | Pass; 48 seed corpus entries loaded |\n| Scoped tracecheck 1.6, 10.1–10.4, 17.3 | 0 | `assigned_scopes=6` |\n| Catalog generated-output check | 0 | Pass |\n| `go build ./...` | 0 | Pass |\n| `go vet ./...` | 0 | Pass |\n| Linux amd64 canonicaljson test cross-compile | 0 | Pass |\n| Windows amd64 canonicaljson test cross-compile | 0 | Pass |\n| `gofmt -l internal` | 0 | Empty output |\n| `git diff --check` | 0 | Pass |\n| `task-board validate` | 0 | 262 inherited `MISSING_ACTIVITY` diagnostics; current task absent |\n\n## Scope boundary\n\nThis package is read-only and deterministic, so crash/idempotency evidence for\ndurable mutation is not applicable. Section 17.3 evidence covers only the\nimmutable migrated-from identity contribution. It does not claim migration\npublication, atomic reference advancement, rollback retention, `ax migrate`,\n`ax doctor`, or a runtime capability.\n\n"},"/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-2wdm5e/worktree/.temp/TASK-260830-8x76g1/TASK-260830-8x76g1_rework-rev4-logbook.md":{"type":"add","content":"# TASK-260830-8x76g1 — rework revision 4 logbook\n\n- Pinned source read locally from spec commit\n  `28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c`; no unpinned specification text\n  was used.\n- CR revision 3's failure class was broader than its seven examples: member\n  names were closed, but most nested values, unions, ordering and cross-field\n  rules were not validated.\n- Expected-red evidence was captured before implementation. The production\n  entry test exited 1 because 21/21 malformed nested candidates were attested.\n- Reused `internal/scalar` for path, UUID, timestamp and digest rules; added\n  production scalar types for Git OIDs, refs and sanitized URLs rather than\n  embedding looser regular expressions in `closed_shapes.go`.\n- Kept candidate-local validation separate from facts that require referenced\n  bytes: Blob Descriptor equality, child-manifest closure, raw Git pack/index\n  agreement, isolated object-database resolution, and filesystem resolution.\n  README now states that boundary explicitly.\n- The recursive submodule validator now checks initialized/uninitialized state,\n  TM-GIT parent index linkage, object formats, depth 16, total 256, ancestor\n  cycles and sibling path collisions. Exact depth/count positives and narrowed\n  negatives drive both identity entries.\n- Every post-fix test/fuzz/trace/build/vet/cross-compile gate exited 0. Package\n  coverage is 90.1% scalar and 81.5% canonicaljson.\n- `task-board validate` exited 0 while printing 262 inherited\n  `MISSING_ACTIVITY` diagnostics. `TASK-260830-8x76g1` is not among them.\n- No external blocker, product decision, durable mutation, doctor output, or\n  capability advertisement was introduced.\n"}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-2wdm5e/worktree/.temp/TASK-260830-8x76g1/TASK-260830-8x76g1_rework-rev4-results.md\nA /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-2wdm5e/worktree/.temp/TASK-260830-8x76g1/TASK-260830-8x76g1_rework-rev4-logbook.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1788202530601,"completed_at_ms":1788202530602}}
